=== PARITY ===
Reads / queries (1/1 ported):
  [x] useLogStream
        transport: GET /admin/logs/stream  (SSE over the shared S4 SseTransport;
                   transport adds the /api/v1 prefix — matches the resilient client).
                   Uses the transport DIRECTLY (not the auto-reconnecting SseClient) so
                   the holder makes exactly ONE connection — byte-for-byte the web
                   hook's no-auto-reconnect behaviour.
        params   : level (always) ; grep (only when non-blank after trim) — snake_case,
                   form-url-encoded identically to the browser URLSearchParams
                   (space -> '+', unreserved pass-through, else %XX of UTF-8 bytes).
        framing  : shared SseFrameParser reproduces the web parseSSEChunk dispatch
                   (event:/data:, CRLF normalised, multi-line data joined with '\n',
                   blank line = frame boundary, leading-':' comment/heartbeat ignored).
        frames   : log -> append ; drop -> accumulate count ; connected/heartbeat/
                   unnamed -> ignored — identical to the hook's switch.
        derived  : detectLevel (parsed.level when string, else "info") ;
                   buildLogEvent (parsed=null on non-JSON, level falls back to "info") ;
                   rolling buffer FIFO-bounded to LOG_STREAM_MAX_EVENTS=1000 ;
                   totalReceived counts EVERY appended event (incl. later evicted) ;
                   drops accumulate (count>0 guard) ;
                   isConnected toggles true while streaming, false on end/error ;
                   error = transport failure message (cancellation is NOT an error) ;
                   pause = skip log append, keep connection + drop counting ;
                   clear = reset events+drops+totalReceived, KEEP isConnected+error ;
                   no auto-reconnect (single connection).
        rAF      : the web hook's requestAnimationFrame batching is a renderer-only
                   optimisation; folding each frame synchronously yields identical
                   buffer contents + counters, so the data behaviour is preserved.
        SI       : payloads are opaque zerolog log lines — no unit-bearing fields,
                   nothing to convert (S5 N/A).
Mutations / actions: 0/0 (the web hook exposes none).

--- Documented web-parity (NOT silent drift) ---
parseDropCount reads data.count, exactly as the web hook does. The live backend
(internal/api/adminlogstream/handler.go) emits a drop frame keyed missed/total, so
the web hook's drop counter does not advance against the real server. The mandate for
this artifact is parity with the WEB HOOK, so count is reproduced verbatim and the C#
port must match. Reconciling the key name with the backend is a separate web-side
change, out of scope here. Pinned by LogStreamReducerTest.parseDropCountReadsCountFieldOnly
and LogStreamStoreTest.ignoresBackendDropKeysForWebParity.

